---
title: "Community Update #0.0 / Change of plans"
date: '2026-05-21'
description: ''
draft: false
---

Hi there. My name is Misha, I’m on a quest to design a comprehensive process for building tech companies from the ground up, and there’s not gonna be a newsletter this week. Which is a weird thing to say, considering that you are probably reading this in form of an email. But there’s a catch. I’m bearing news. Welcome to our first community update.


Remember me mentioning I’m balancing this whole ordeal with a day job? This recently led me to think long and hard about my priorities. See, I don’t just have to balance this project with a day job, I also need to balance the newsletter with venture work.  Every week I start, finish or prepare an experiment for venture design and/or validation. During the same week I need to prepare, write and publish a newsletter, which I take very seriously. After three weeks of releasing newsletters on Friday afternoon I had to concede that this is very hard to manage and it also creates unnecessary conflicts in my calendar. I’ve mentioned before that I’m prototyping this thing, so changes like this should not come as a surprise, but long story short, I made a decision. Here’s how the content schedule will look from now on: 

1. A community update every Tuesday
2. A newsletter *every other* Thursday

You read this right. From now on, the usual newsletter will arrive roughly twice a month. This will allow me focus more on venture work as well as to pump up the quality of my writing. Thanks for being so understanding. But let’s address the elephant in the room: the hell are community updates? 

Since way before I even started this blog, the project was always going to be social. For the whole experiment to work, I need an active community of like-minded people. I’ll tell you all about the very exciting plans in future updates, what’s important right now is the following: yes, you’re in. And yes, I’m planning for way less one-sided communication. More about that to come. Stay tuned. 

The bi-monthly newsletters will be less focused on the technical details of our journey, rather on findings, methods, insights and other things I found interesting enough to share with the general audience. The progress so far, changelog, interactive activities and other announcements closely related to our venture design methodology and database will now arrive in form of community updates (by the way, If we ever come down to once again asking for your financial support, this is where it’s gonna happen). This  does indeed mean that in order to follow the journey, you need to subscribe. Don’t worry though: I’m not planning to ever hide any piece of content or data behind a paywall and the database will remain free and open forever. 

I know that asking to join and be active in an online community is a big ask, that’s why I’m not asking for anything yet, although I do have quite ambitious plans. And trust me, when the time comes for me asking for your participation of any kind, it’s going to be opt-in. 

This letter will be posted on the [main website](erikov.me), but the future ones, for the most part, will not. It only makes sense: in order to receive community updates, you need to be a member. If you’re reading this in your inbox, congratulations: you already are. If not, click that subscribe button. It’s gonna be fun. 

My name is Misha and I’ll see you on Tuesday.
Be brave. Be stupid. And [don’t be a stranger](mailto:erikov@hey.com).

Cheers.







